  "question": {
    "text": "If $P(x)=a x^2+b x+c$ and $Q(x)=-a x^2+d x+c$ where $a c \\neq 0$, then $P(x) \\cdot Q(x)=0$ has $(a, b, c, d$ are real)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TpxZh",
      "text": "2 real roots",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "92XDn",
      "text": "at least two real roots",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "wI4BQ",
      "text": "4 real roots",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JpAvV",
      "text": "no real root",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { Hint: } D_1=b^2-4 a c \\\\\n& D_2=d^2+4 a c \\\\\n& D_1+D_2=b^2+d^2\\gt0 \\\\\n& D_1+D_2\\gt0\n\\end{aligned}$\nAt least one of $D_1$ or $D_2$ is +ve so at least two real roots",
    "image": null
  },
